          "malayalam": ""
        },
        "note": {
          "english": "Clear answers for operations, finance and lean IT teams.",
          "malayalam": ""
        },
        "linkLabel": {
          "english": "",
          "malayalam": ""
        },
        "linkUrl": {
          "english": "",
          "malayalam": ""
        },
        "rows": {
          "lastUUID": 6,
          "items": [
            {
              "id": 1,
              "item": {
                "title": {
                  "english": "We run different ERPs across acquired plants and older PLCs on the shop floor. Do we need to standardise them first?",
                  "malayalam": ""
                },
                "anchor": {
                  "english": "",
                  "malayalam": ""
                },
                "body": {
                  "english": "No. Your ERPs, MES and shop-floor systems stay as they are. Spontaine reads from each of them and agrees what margin, cost and on-time mean across every plant, so nothing has to be standardised first.",
                  "malayalam": ""
                },
                "entries": {
                  "lastUUID": 0,
                  "items": []
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "id": 2,
              "item": {
                "title": {
                  "english": "Our IT team is small and focused on keeping plants running. How much internal engineering does this require?",
                  "malayalam": ""
                },
                "anchor": {
                  "english": "",
                  "malayalam": ""
                },
                "body": {
                  "english": "Very little. IT grants read access to the systems that hold the answer and chooses where Spontaine runs. We do the connecting and the modelling. IT owns the perimeter. Not the backlog.",
                  "malayalam": ""
                },
                "entries": {
                  "lastUUID": 0,
                  "items": []
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "id": 3,
              "item": {
                "title": {
                  "english": "How is this different from building a data warehouse in Snowflake or hiring a systems integrator?",
                  "malayalam": ""
                },
                "anchor": {
                  "english": "",
                  "malayalam": ""
                },
                "body": {
                  "english": "A warehouse stores data. Someone still has to model it, agree the definitions and build every answer on top, and that is where integrator projects run for years. Spontaine arrives with that layer: connections, agreed definitions and live answers, delivered in weeks on a fixed scope and fee. If you already run a warehouse, Spontaine reads from it too.",
                  "malayalam": ""
                },
                "entries": {
                  "lastUUID": 0,
                  "items": []
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "id": 4,
              "item": {
                "title": {
                  "english": "How do you capture shop-floor data without disrupting active production lines?",
                  "malayalam": ""
                },
                "anchor": {
                  "english": "",
                  "malayalam": ""
                },
                "body": {
                  "english": "We read from the systems that already record it, such as your MES, historians and machine data collection, rather than touching the lines themselves. Nothing on the floor is reconfigured, and no line has to stop.",
                  "malayalam": ""
                },
                "entries": {
                  "lastUUID": 0,
                  "items": []
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "id": 5,
              "item": {
                "title": {
                  "english": "Can we push live production and margin data back into our CRM and customer portals without custom APIs?",
                  "malayalam": ""
                },
                "anchor": {
                  "english": "",
                  "malayalam": ""
                },
                "body": {
                  "english": "Yes. Every governed dataset in Spontaine is already a secure API. Send it to your CRM, or give a customer a portal scoped to exactly what they may see. Nothing else leaves.",
                  "malayalam": ""
                },
                "entries": {
                  "lastUUID": 0,
                  "items": []
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "id": 6,
              "item": {
                "title": {
                  "english": "What does a first four-week deployment cost and deliver?",
                  "malayalam": ""
                },
                "anchor": {
                  "english": "",
                  "malayalam": ""
                },
                "body": {
                  "english": "One cross-system question answered from your own systems and refreshing on its own, with the definitions agreed by your team. Fixed scope and fixed fee, agreed before we start; we quote once we know the question and the systems. If you stop, the data and results stay yours.",
                  "malayalam": ""
                },
                "entries": {
                  "lastUUID": 0,
                  "items": []
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
